# Bot2's Anointed Peacekeeper names Illusionary Mask, so its ability costs {2} more (CR 601.2f): on turn 3 Bot1 activates it
# for X = 2 and pays {W}{B}{U}{G}, all four (the pool empty after). No part of that mana is told apart as X's: a creature card
# qualifies if at most X of the mana spent could pay its mana cost, in any combination (owner ruling 2026-11-27). Balduvian
# Bears' {1}{G} is paid by two of it - the {G} and any other - and may be chosen; Wildwood Patrol's {2}{G} would take three,
# more than X, though four were spent, and may not.

